# System Architecture

## Overview

The Veridian IT Support Agent follows a modular architecture that separates the user interface, request routing, policy retrieval, deterministic policy evaluation, risk assessment, ticket generation, and audit logging.

The architecture is designed so that the LLM assists with natural-language understanding and response generation, while policy and risk decisions are handled through deterministic logic grounded in the supplied Veridian Corp. knowledge base.

## Architecture Diagram

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Streamlit UI"] --> B["Agent Router"]
    B --> C["LLM Handler"]
    B --> D["Policy Engine"]
    B --> E["Risk Engine"]
    B --> F["Ticket Generator"]
    B --> G["Audit Logger"]
    D --> H["Policy Retriever"]
    H --> I["Knowledge Base (JSON)"]

    C -.-> I
